---
description: Never read or modify .env unless user explicitly asks
alwaysApply: true
---

# Do not access `.env`

- Never read `.env` or any `*.env` file (including variants like `.env.local`, `.env.production`, etc.).
- Never create, modify, delete, or rename `.env` / `*.env` files.
- If environment variables are needed, only:
  - instruct the user what to put in `.env` (in plain text), or
  - update `.env.example` / docs (safe templates), unless the user says otherwise.

# Exceptions

- Only touch `.env` / `*.env` if the user explicitly requests it in the current conversation.
